---
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const moduleUsage = `<wf-lockxy-panel></wf-lockxy-panel>
<script type="module">
  import '@wesflo/lockxy-panel';
</script>`;

const scriptUsage = `<wf-lockxy-panel></wf-lockxy-panel>
<script src="./node_modules/@wesflo/lockxy-panel/dist/wf-lockxy-panel.umd.cjs"></script>`;
---

<DocsLayout title="Proxy panel" description="Embed and operate the optional Lockxy proxy panel." activePath="/proxy-panel/">
    <article>
        <p class="kicker">Optional browser controls</p>
        <h1>Switch manifest behavior without changing files.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            The plugin works without the panel. Add it when a manifest defines multiple behaviors per URL and developers
            should be able to select them—or bypass individual endpoints—directly in the browser.
        </p>

        <h2 id="module-integration">Module integration</h2>
        <Code code={moduleUsage} label="index.html" />

        <h2 id="classic-script-integration">Classic script integration</h2>
        <Code code={scriptUsage} label="index.html" />
        <p>The UMD build is self-contained. The package also publishes an ES module and TypeScript declarations.</p>

        <h2 id="controls">Controls</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Click the floating launcher to open or close the panel.</li>
            <li>Press <code>Escape</code> to close it and return focus to the launcher.</li>
            <li>Hold <code>Ctrl</code> or <code>Cmd</code> while dragging to move the launcher.</li>
            <li>The launcher position is stored in local storage and restored on the next visit.</li>
            <li>Disable the master switch to pass every API request to the next Vite middleware.</li>
            <li>Disable an endpoint switch to pass through only that manifest endpoint.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="bypass-cookie">Bypass cookie</h2>
        <Code code={`document.cookie = 'wesflo-mock-api-bypass=*; Path=/; SameSite=Lax';`} label="bypass all mocks" />
        <Code
            code={`document.cookie = 'wesflo-mock-api-bypass=orders|user-profile; Path=/; SameSite=Lax';`}
            label="bypass selected endpoint IDs"
        />
        <Callout title="Passthrough behavior">
            <p>
                Bypass does not perform the remote request itself. It calls the next Vite middleware, so configure
                <code>server.proxy</code> when requests should continue to a development API.
            </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="settings-and-persistence">Settings and persistence</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Enable proxy on load</strong> is enabled by default and stored in local storage. When disabled, mounting
            the panel creates a global bypass only when no bypass cookie exists yet. Existing cookie state always wins on a
            reload. Changing the setting still updates the current cookie immediately.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Save selections in local storage</strong> is disabled by default. When enabled, individual endpoint
            bypasses and scenario choices are stored below the manifest's root <code>id</code> and by normalized HTTP method
            and path, for example <code>checkout → GET /api/orders</code>. The setting is unavailable without a root ID, so
            unrelated micro frontends cannot accidentally share these values. The panel maps stored values back to the
            current endpoint IDs after loading. If a selected scenario no longer exists, the first configured scenario is
            used as a fallback.
        </p>
        <Callout title="Shared-origin limitation">
            <p>
                Local storage is shared by applications on the same origin, which is why Lockxy requires a manifest root ID
                before storing selections. Use <strong>Reset all settings</strong> to remove all panel-owned project
                selections, preferences, cookies, and the saved launcher position.
            </p>
        </Callout>

        <Callout title="Cookies survive reloads">
            <p>
                Mounting the panel preserves valid bypass and scenario cookies and initializes every scenario select from
                the cookie. After a project switch, entries that do not exist in the current manifest are removed; a stale
                scenario falls back to that endpoint's first scenario. Explicitly resetting the panel still clears all
                Lockxy state.
            </p>
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="scenario-cookie">Scenario cookie</h2>
        <p>
            Scenario selections use <code>wesflo-mock-api-scenarios</code>. Entries are encoded as
            <code>endpoint-id:scenario-id</code> and separated with <code>|</code>. Prefer the panel or the exported utility
            helpers over constructing this value manually. If a stored scenario no longer exists after the manifest is
            changed, the endpoint automatically uses its first configured scenario.
        </p>
    </article>
</DocsLayout>
